<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Q2 industrial production falls.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Q2 industrial production falls.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian industrial production fell 1.0 percent in seasonally adjusted terms in the June quarter, the Australian Bureau of Statistics (ABS) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Despite the June quarter fall, industrial production was up 3.2 percent over the past year, the ABS said.  </p>
<p>In original terms industrial production rose 2.4 percent in the quarter, while the trend series showed a 0.6 percent rise.</p>
<p>Industrial Production index, seasonally adjusted gross product at 1989/90 prices</p>
<p>					  qtr/qtr  June Index   June/June</p>
<p>    Mining(ex services)	    +0.7	 122.1	 +7.4</p>
<p>    Manufacturing		    -1.6	 108.3	 +2.5</p>
<p>    Electricity, gas, water	-0.3	 110.9	 +0.5</p>
<p>    Total Industrial		 -1.0	 111.2	 +3.2</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
